# Mutations for mutate.py. Each one swaps a piece of MatrixBlocks.lean for a
# plausible bug. The text after `- ` must occur exactly once in the model;
# `+ ` lines replace it. mutate.py reports the declarations that fail on each.

mutation zero block rows
- max 1 (values / columns)
+ values / columns

mutation uncapped workers
- min requested ((rows + block - 1) / block)
+ max requested ((rows + block - 1) / block)

mutation floor instead of ceiling
- min requested ((rows + block - 1) / block)
+ min requested (rows / block)

mutation advance one row short
- min rows (start + block)
+ min rows (start + block - 1)

mutation undersized capacity
- min rows block * columns * bytes
+ (min rows block - 1) * columns * bytes
